{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Therefore say to the children of Israel: I am YHWH.</b> For all these three reasons, say to the children of Israel that I am He who grants present existence to all existing things, and by this power I shall bring them out — for I shall change somewhat of their nature." "<b>And I shall bring you out from under the burdens of Egypt.</b> From the day the plagues begin, the subjugation shall cease." "<b>And I shall rescue you.</b> On the day of your departure, when you go forth from their border." "<b>And I shall redeem you.</b> In the drowning of the Egyptians in the sea, as He testified in saying: וַיּוֹשַׁע ה' בַּיּוֹם הַהוּא וְכוּ׳ (Exodus 14:30) — for after the death of the enslavers, they were no longer fleeing slaves."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:34.140522334Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}